    "description": "Client-owed inputs, tracked so an unassigned owner does not silently become the schedule.\n\n\\[POC\\] needed to start:\n\n* C1 Google Cloud project with the Drive API enabled — nothing can begin without this\n\n* C2 A service account created in that project — the identity Salesforce authenticates as\n\n* C3 Confirmation the Google org policy PERMITS SERVICE-ACCOUNT KEYS. Many enterprise tenants block these by default. Alternatives exist but add effort — we would come back with options rather than proceed\n\n* C4 The service-account credential made available to us. 1Password shared vault is our usual route; equally happy to have their admin paste it straight into Salesforce on a screenshare. NEVER over email or chat\n\n* C5 A NAMED Google Workspace admin who can action C1-C7, plus a target date. The single biggest schedule risk on this work is an unassigned owner, not the build\n\n* C6 A test SHARED DRIVE the service account can write to — must be a Shared Drive, NOT a folder in someone's personal Drive. A service account has no usable storage allowance of its own so uploads to a personal Drive fail on quota\n\n* C7 Confirmation of maximum file size and accepted file types. Working assumption is short phone recordings, 10-20s, a few MB to \\~50MB\n\n\\[Build\\] needed only on a go decision:\n\n* C8 A permanent Shared Drive for production proofs, service account as Content Manager, their admins as Managers, reps added as members. Rep membership is what gives reps the ability to open proof links\n\nSource: Drive Storage doc §5, §11.",
